==Old Norse==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*skrahō||dry animal skin}}, of {{unc|non|nocap=1}} origin, though possibly a derivative of {{inh|non|ine-pro|*(s)ker-|t=to shrink, dry, wrinkle, bend}}.<ref name=AnEW>{{R:non:AnEW|pages=500-1|head=skrá 1}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:IEW|2693}}</ref> {{rfe|non|Pokorny reference doesn't point to correct section - this should be fixed.}} Related to dialectal Norwegian {{m|no|skråen||half-dried, withered, hard}}, {{cog|gml|schra||dry, lean}}, {{cog|urj-fin-pro|*raha|t=squirrel pelt; money}}.<ref name=AnEW /> Note in particular similarities to {{cog|gem-pro|*skrinkwaną|t=to shrink}}.

====Noun====
{{non-noun|f}}

# [[dried]] [[skin]], [[parchment]]
# [[scroll]], written [[document]]

